       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4,250 mg three times daily (12,750 mg/day) has no therapeutic use for metformin. A single 4,250 mg dose is already near the range where metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis are a concern. Normal kidney and liver function won't make that dose safe.\n\nYou have other ways to get an order like this placed:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or any other dose within labeled limits.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If you have a specific clinical reason for a dose outside labeled limits, such as a protocol or trial, the clinical pharmacist can review it and co-sign. You can also enter it directly in the order system with that documentation.\n- **Check for an error.** If the dose came from a calculation or a template, it may be worth rechecking the source.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
